Compute policies types:

	Personal Compute
		Allows users to create an individually assigned single node compute resource with minimal configurations, intended for single user.
		
	Job compute
		Allows to create a general purpose default compute for jobs
		
	Legacy shared compute
		
	Shared compute
		Allows to create larger multi node resources, intended for multiple users to share
		
	Power user compute
		Allows to create larger  multi node clusters. intended for single user workloads which require more resources.



Custom policy
we can create a custom policy, this mostly inherites the configurations from the policy types which we can choose from the policy family.
Custom policy are helfull when we need to restrct users on some options like termination time, runtime, node type.

Under the compute tab in policies we can see which cluster are using the current policy
compute -> policies ->compute tab

Permissions on compute:
	Can attach to -- allows you to attach your notebook to the compute
	Can restart     -- allows to start,restart and terminate the compute including attach permissions
	Can Manage  -- allows to edit the compute details, permissions and size, including both attach and restart permissions
	
	Attach -- Attach
	Restart -- Restart + Attach
	Manage -- Manage + Restart + Attach


